","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Bayrisch Kraut (Bavarian cabbage) is a traditional Bavarian dish. It is made of shredded cabbage cooked in beef stock with pork lard, onion, apples, and seasoned with salt, black pepper, caraway, sugar and vinegar. It is typically served with bratwurst or roast pork. In German cuisine it is an alternative to sauerkraut."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bayrisch-kraut"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayrisch_Kraut"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bavarian cuisine","cuisine/bavarian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Apple","ingredient/apple"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]},{"h":"More from Bavarian cuisine","links":[["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Rumford's Soup","dish/rumford-s-soup"],["Weißwurst","dish/wei-wurst"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/cf/Speckkn%C3%B6del_auf_Kraut%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Speckkn%C3%B6del_auf_Kraut%2C_2013.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Christian Allinger","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Speckkn%C3%B6del_auf_Kraut%2C_2013.jpg"}},"dish/blanquette-de-veau":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/blanquette-de-veau","n":"Blanquette de veau","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Blanquette de veau is a French veal stew. In the classic version of the dish the meat is simmered in a white stock and served in a sauce velouté enriched with cream and egg."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-blanquette-de-veau"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanquette_de_veau"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Mirepoix","ingredient/mirepoix"],["Mirepoix (cuisine)","ingredient/mirepoix-cu